<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#reichskommissar">Glossary</a> · Term · office</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reichskommissar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Reich Commissioner</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A Reichskommissar, or Reich Commissioner, was in Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> an official appointed to govern an occupied territory as a civil administrator answerable directly to Hitler. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> Reichskommissariats were set up in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, Ostland and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, headed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josef-terboven">Josef Terboven</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arthur-seyss-inquart">Arthur Seyss-Inquart</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinrich-lohse">Hinrich Lohse</a> and Erich Koch.</p></div>
